1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Yakant Idol 

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Well, it's early and it's the ending.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Do you have any news from Mr. Serif?

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Yes, I do. I have an announcement,

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
On Wednesday, June 21, we will be releasing our first major single.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Since we are releasing it, JESS is currently in the middle of its release event period,

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,500
I'll be in Kanto and other cities,

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,500
I hope you have a chance to come to the Kanto area,

9
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:30,500
If you have a chance to come to Kanto or if you live near Kanto, please come and play with us.

10
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,000
Wow, what kind of song is it? What kind of songs are they?

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,500
All of them are in the style of "Ukka",

12
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,000
But there are songs that push me forward,

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,200
There was one song that I thought was very difficult when I sang it,

14
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,300
What is the word for that?

15
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,800
How would you put it?

16
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,000
Natural?

17
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,200
What's the word?

18
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,400
I don't know.

19
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,600
There's a song that has a natural feel to it,

20
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,000
A song that feels natural?

21
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,800
Or a song that pushes you forward.

22
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,200
Songs that push you,

23
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,000
Do you have a song that pushes you?

24
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Something natural.

25
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Like, "Just keep your feet on the floor" or something like that?

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Recording was difficult for me.

27
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
But I think it will grow and develop over the course of the release period,

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
I hope you can see that.

29
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,600
I would like you to see that.

30
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:30,600
So it becomes an event even if you are performing live with your fans?

31
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,600
That's right. We do fan live shows and take two-shots.

32
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,000
Taking two-shots.

33
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,400
Smudgeon.

34
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,400
Yes, that's right. I understand.

35
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,600
Now, then...

36
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,200
Yes. I'll be doing a one-man show.

37
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:43,800
What?

38
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,000
September 30, Shibuya Beats.

39
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
October 14, Saturday, Tokyo Kinema Club.

40
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
After the new year, it will be at Ebisu Liquid Room on Sunday, January 21 next year.

41
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Great!

42
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Will each of the three have a different concept?

43
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,300
It's still a ways off.

44
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:13,000
The common goal for all three shows is to sell out every show,

45
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Sell out all the shows.

46
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,500
That's the goal,

47
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:24,500
